    <Notes ShowOnLoad="0" Notes="TCE1:TCE-SC-20261014-C1&#10;Hardware: JPT YDFLP-E-60-M7-M-R 60 W, serial MC2BDJD71684; lens: F-Theta 174 mm; material: titanium (link the exact grade and batch in the experiment record).&#10;Pulse-width capability check for JPT YDFLP-E-60-M7-M-R. Each non-CW pulse step (2..500 ns) has three 10 mm LightBurn Line strokes at 0.8x/1.0x/1.2x the model's listed cut-off frequency. The 1 ns CW setting is included as a reference at F48 kHz. Fixed P20%, V900 mm/s and one pass. Compare whether the titanium response changes near each listed knee; the cut-off values are the device passport model, while these lines are the physical check. This plate tests pulse/frequency behavior, not color.&#10;Canvas 76 x 57 mm; registered bounds 98 x 94.5 mm. First: full-area cross-hatched cleaning, 20% / 48 kHz / 2000 mm/s / 200 ns / 0.05 mm; second: black marker/label layer 25% / 60 kHz / 150 mm/s / 200 ns / 0.01 mm, one pass."/>
</LightBurnProject>
